[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246440187","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110205#issuecomment-3246440187","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110205","id":3246440187,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BgL77","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T18:51:51Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T18:52:33Z","body":"I think there's also another case where you initialize with Variant(), but I haven't checked in gdscript, it's a thing in c++. It's the godot variation of null ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246440187/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3563903797","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110205#issuecomment-3563903797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110205","id":3563903797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UbNs1","user":{"login":"YashwanthCB","id":22799310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNzk5MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22799310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB","html_url":"https://github.com/YashwanthCB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-21T17:03:13Z","updated_at":"2025-11-21T17:03:13Z","body":"> I think there's also another case where you initialize with Variant(), but I haven't checked in gdscript, it's a thing in c++. It's the godot variation of null\n\ni am getting error when i try to initialize like this `var t = Variant()`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3563903797/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3564111576","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110205#issuecomment-3564111576","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110205","id":3564111576,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UcAbY","user":{"login":"YashwanthCB","id":22799310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNzk5MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22799310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB","html_url":"https://github.com/YashwanthCB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-21T18:07:32Z","updated_at":"2025-11-21T18:08:36Z","body":"I have some behavioral questions. We declare a variable like this: `@export var m_with_type_with_default: Variant = \"m_with_type_with_default\"` and change the value in the editor. What will be the effect when i compile the script again with\n1. same value\n2. different value\n3. different type in initialization like `= 3` or `= 5.6` etc..\n\nDo we have any document for gdscript that explains what happens in such scenarios?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3564111576/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3564274219","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110205#issuecomment-3564274219","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110205","id":3564274219,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UcoIr","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-21T19:07:29Z","updated_at":"2025-11-21T19:07:29Z","body":"I wanted to fix this before the 4.5 release, but unfortunately I have little free time. Please note the following:\n\n```gdscript\n# 1. Correct. The only one of the 4 cases where the type switch appears\n# in the editor at the moment.\n@export var m_with_type_without_default: Variant\n# 2. Incorrect. The weak type `String` is deduced, but the variable\n# is explicitly annotated with the static type `Variant`\n@export var m_with_type_with_default: Variant = 'm_with_type_with_default'\n# 3. Correct (!?). The weak type `String` is deduced.\n# This is how untyped exports work before, the change would be a compatibility break.\n@export var m_without_type_with_default = 'm_without_type_with_default'\n# 4. Incorrect. Currently not allowed, but should be permitted.\n@export var m_without_type_without_default\n```\n\nWhile cases 2 and 4 are more or less obvious and the change is expected, in case 3 we can't change the current behavior for compatibility reasons with the old behavior and support for untyped code (type hints shouldn't be mandatory).\n\nHowever, the difference in behavior between cases 2 and 3 also seems somewhat inconsistent.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3564274219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3565818999","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110205#issuecomment-3565818999","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110205","id":3565818999,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UihR3","user":{"login":"YashwanthCB","id":22799310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNzk5MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22799310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB","html_url":"https://github.com/YashwanthCB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T06:29:00Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T06:29:00Z","body":"I am working on this issue. Will keep you posted.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3565818999/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566554124","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110205#issuecomment-3566554124","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110205","id":3566554124,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UlUwM","user":{"login":"YashwanthCB","id":22799310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNzk5MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22799310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB","html_url":"https://github.com/YashwanthCB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T11:08:44Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T11:08:44Z","body":"So far, I have changed the behavior for explicit annotation and weak type `@export var m_with_type_with_default: Variant = 'm_with_type_with_default'`. It was a really easy fix.\n\n<img width=\"1415\" height=\"226\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4a3f47fe-0b83-4933-a82d-a0d7b2166d7d\" />\n\n<img width=\"1424\" height=\"892\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d0c91a2b-c808-4e3b-ac12-d91f4dfe99d7\" />\n\nYou can change it to any type you want. \n\n<img width=\"1410\" height=\"390\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a7009802-3e14-4fcd-8649-012aa02552df\" />\n\nBut does not work for all types \n\n<img width=\"581\" height=\"117\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cb8bb426-c52f-4e26-a10d-8846c080c756\" />\n\nWhen i change it to any type of Array(normal, packed variations) or dictionary, it simply returns Nil as type. In order to make it work, i have to switch between any non-nullable types(like bool or int) and Array to let the editor assign the proper value like this:\n\n<img width=\"579\" height=\"156\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/680ba660-c513-4bcb-bf6a-23805b4b5eab\" />\nBut this won't work every time. Sometimes it will remain Nil how much ever times you try to fix it.\n\nThis seems to be fairly complex topic and it will take more time. \nSo I am requesting the maintainers to change the Complexity to Medium or above.\n\nI am gonna keep working on it anyway and post the changes here.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566554124/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566645970","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110205#issuecomment-3566645970","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110205","id":3566645970,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UlrLS","user":{"login":"YashwanthCB","id":22799310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNzk5MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22799310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB","html_url":"https://github.com/YashwanthCB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashwanthCB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T11:52:05Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T17:53:07Z","body":"Well I feel dumb for not noticing one thing. If you cast the initializer to Variant, the Variant editor pops up without issues.\n`@export var test1 = 4 as Variant` results in this:\n\n<img width=\"537\" height=\"31\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cd655698-d6f4-43ab-99fc-e494a1ac60d5\" />\n\nFor this I don't need to modify any engine code. It already works the way it is intended.\n\nThis can be considered as work-around but I still need expert's view on how we fix the GDScript grammar in this case.\n\nRegardless the initialization bug for Array-like types and Dictionary still prevails as i mentioned in previous comment:\n\n<img width=\"530\" height=\"38\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/05d91fb2-c182-4c4b-bd13-18bd64bc1b25\" />\n\nI feel that this is an issue with Editor processing export properties and not gdscript language or parser itself.\nIt is better to add topic:editor label too.\n\nHowever, whether the variable in `@export var test1 :  Variant = 4` should be treated as Variant type is still debatable. \n\nSo, I am requesting guidance from experts.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566645970/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]